ce generation] The target video is a 44.8-second cinematic Chinese-language wuxia music video (segment 2 of 2). <Subject 1> sings the supplied driving audio track on camera, his lip movement articulated syllable-by-syllable in sync with that driving audio, across five alternating locations: a candle-lit inn at dawn, a rain-washed alley, a moon-white mist field, a wind-scoured field at a cliff edge at dusk, and a final moonlit cliff. The segment covers the second half of the first verse, then two full choruses, and closes with a long instrumental outro. Cuts, flash-whites, and strobe accents land on the musical beat, and the picture stays in a 2.39:1 anamorphic, 24 fps, film-grained, shallow-depth-of-field, backlit wuxia-cinematic style with ink-wash color language alternating cool moon-white, warm amber, and deep crimson. **No weapons appear anywhere in the frame.**\n\n**retention_analysis:**\n\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1] through [Shot 8]): fully_preserved - his facial identity, the high ponytail with leather cord, the ink-black robe with crimson inner layers, and his proud, lonely bearing are retained in every shot, with only lighting and color grading changing between locations. His hands remain empty and natural throughout; no weapon or extra hand appears in any shot.\nThe supplied driving audio track (connected outside this prompt as the driving audio, not referenced by an in-prompt label): fully_copy - the complete driving audio track is reused 1:1 as the target video's complete final audio track, and <Subject 1>'s lip movement is articulated syllable-by-syllable in sync with it.\n\n**detailed_description:**\n\nThe target video is a live-action cinematic wuxia music video in a 2.39:1 anamorphic frame at 24 fps, with shallow depth of field, visible fine film grain, strong backlit rim lighting, and an ink-wash color language alternating cold moon-white, warm amber, and deep crimson. <Subject 1> sings on camera from 00:02 onward, and in every singing shot his lips, teeth, and jaw articulate syllable-by-syllable in exact sync with the supplied driving audio track. **No weapons, swords, blades, or props appear; his hands are always empty, natural, and rarely prominent in frame.**\n\n[Shot 1] The segment opens on the dim inn interior from the previous segment, the amber candle now burned low. A low drum hits at 00:00.000 and the shot holds on the guttering flame for the two-second drum intro; <Subject 1> (S1), a young wuxia singer with a resonant, gravelly-edged tenor voice and the appearance referenced from <Picture 1>, lifts his head slowly, lips closed and jaw still. At 00:02.200 a hard cut lands as he begins to sing.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.200, a jump-cut tightens onto his face in the candle-lit inn. <Subject 1> (S1) sings <d>[Chinese] 恩和怨 是幻是空</d> at 00:02.200 with his mouth opening on the first syllable and closing softly on the last, his eyes unfocused, and <d>[Chinese] 我醒 一场春梦</d> at 00:04.200 with his jaw dropping on the long middle vowel before closing softly. The candle flares behind his face as the camera pushes in.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:07.800, pale dawn light falls through the lattice window and the shot widens. <Subject 1> (S1) sits at the table, the empty wine bowl before him, hands resting empty on the tabletop. He sings <d>[Chinese] 生与死 一切成空</d> at 00:09.500 with his lips rounding and narrowing on the final soft vowel, then falls silent as the camera pulls back to reveal misty mountains through the window. A rapid drum roll builds and a flash-white lands on the downbeat at 00:11.100.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:11.100, a rapid jump-cut lands on the downbeat as the chorus begins. <Subject 1> (S1) runs through a rain-washed old alley under amber street lamps, robes and ponytail streaming behind him, his hands empty and swinging naturally at his sides. He sings <d>[Chinese] 来也匆匆 去也匆匆 恨不能相逢</d> at 00:11.100 with his mouth opening cleanly on each phrase and his jaw bobbing on the beat, and <d>[Chinese] 爱也匆匆 恨也匆匆 一切都随风</d> at 00:16.300 with strong, even articulation as he slows to a stop. The camera tracks alongside him at running pace, the lamps flaring past in long streaks.\n\n[Shot 5] At 00:19.900, a strobe-accented cut moves to the top of the highest rooftop under the night sky. <Subject 1> (S1) throws his head back and sings out across the city, <d>[Chinese] 狂笑一声 长叹一声 快活一生 悲哀一生</d> at 00:19.900, his mouth opening wide and his jaw dropping fully on each sustained vowel, a wild, laughing edge to the phrase, then a sudden stillness as he lowers his gaze, and <d>[Chinese] 谁与我生死与共</d> at 00:25.000 with his lips finishing the phrase and holding. The camera performs an arc shot with large amplitude around him at a steady pace, the city lights strobing across the lens. A flash-white lands at 00:30.900.\n\n[Shot 6] At 00:30.900, the chorus repeats with a flash-white transition onto a moon-white mist field where dark figures stand in ranks at the edges of the frame. <Subject 1> (S1) walks slowly through them, alone, hands resting at his sides, robes and ponytail moving in the wind. He sings <d>[Chinese] 来也匆匆 去也匆匆 恨不能相逢</d> at 00:30.900 with crisp lip closure on each phrase, and <d>[Chinese] 爱也匆匆 恨也匆匆 一切都随风</d> at 00:34.500 as the figures dissolve into mist behind him. The camera pulls back slowly.\n\n[Shot 7] At 00:37.800, a strobe-accented cut moves to a wind-scoured field at the edge of a cliff under a blood-red dusk sky. <Subject 1> (S1) stands alone, robes and ponytail streaming in the wind, hands empty and relaxed at his sides. He sings <d>[Chinese] 狂笑一声 长叹一声 快活一生 悲哀一生</d> at 00:37.800 with a wide, sustained jaw drop on each phrase, and <d>[Chinese] 谁与我生死与共</d> at 00:41.800 with his eyes closing on the first word while his lips keep articulating, the final vowel drawing out long into the wind until 00:44.800. The camera pulls back slowly, the field dissolving into mist behind him.\n\n[Shot 8] At 00:44.800, the picture holds on the empty cliff as the instrumental outro plays: <Subject 1>